Notes on code this block builds on

- The Kuwahara filter (Kuwahara et al., 1976) is a classic published image filter; the 4-sector version here was
  written fresh in GLSL.
- The ACES curve in grade.js is the widely used fitted approximation (RRT+ODT fit by Stephen Hill, MIT licence).
- NeutralToneMapping comes from three.js's own shader chunk (Khronos PBR Neutral, three.js MIT licence).
- The small hash and value-noise one-liners (fract/sin and fract/dot hashes) are common public snippets.
- three.js and its addons (FullScreenQuad, UnrealBloomPass) are MIT licensed, Copyright 2010-2026 three.js authors.
